          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Kan extension
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to D
            with respect to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  C
                  \\\
                  \\big\downarrow\mathrlap{{}^p}
                  \\\
                  C'
                  }
          %p
            is, if it exists, a kind of
            %em best approximation
            to the problem of finding a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C' \to D
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi F
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mi p
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo ′
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  C &amp;\stackrel{F}{\to}&amp; D
                  \\\
                  \\mathllap{{}^p}\big\downarrow &amp; \nearrow
                  \\\
                  C'
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            hence to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extending
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
          %p
            More generally, this notion makes sense not only in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            but in any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
          %p
            Similarly, a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+lift"} Kan lift
            is the best approximation to lifting a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to D
            through a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                          %mo ′
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  D'
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow
                  \\\
                  D
                  }
          %p
            to a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat F
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                          %mo ′
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mover
                              %mi F
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi F
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; D'
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\hat F}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  C &amp;\stackrel{F}{\to}&amp; D
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Kan extensions are ubiquitous. See the discussion at
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Examples"} Examples
            below.
          %h2#Definitions Definitions
          %p
            There are various slight variants of the definition of
            = succeed "." do
              %em Kan extension
          %p We (have to) distinguish the following cases:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#OrdinaryKanExtensions"} “ordinary” or “weak” Kan extensions
              %p
                These define the extension of an entire functor, by an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjointness
                relation.
              %p Here we (have to) distinguish further between
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %a{:href => "#GlobalKanExtensions"}> global Kan extensions
                    ,
                  %p
                    which define extensions of
                    %em all
                    possible functors of given domain and codomain (if all of them indeed exist);
                %li
                  %p
                    %a{:href => "#LocalKanExtensions"}> local Kan extensions
                    ,
                  %p which define extensions of single functors only, which may exist even if not every functor has an extension.
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Pointwise"} “pointwise” Kan extensions
              %p
                These define the
                %em value
                of an extended functor on each object (each “point”) by a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted (co)limit
              %p
                Furthermore, a pointwise Kan extension can be
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#AbsoluteKanExtension"} “absolute”
          %p
            If the pointwise version exists, then it coincides with the “ordinary” or “weak” version, but the former may exist without the pointwise version existing. See
            %a{:href => "#pointwiseVsWeak"} below
            for more.
          %p
            Some authors (such as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Kelly"} Kelly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            theory.
          %h3#OrdinaryKanExtensions Ordinary or weak Kan extensions
          %h4#GlobalKanExtensions Global Kan extensions
          %p Let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p : C \to C'
          %p
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            any other category, write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p^* : [C',D] \to [C,D]
          %p
            for the induced functor on the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+categories"} functor categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : C' \to D
            to the composite functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi p
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi h
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^* h : C \stackrel{p}{\to} C' \stackrel{h}{\to} D
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
              has a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p_! : [C,D] \to [C',D]
            %p or
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Lan_p : [C,D] \to [C',D]
            %p
              then this left adjoint is called the (
              %em ordinary
              or
              %em weak
              )
              %strong left Kan extension
              operation along
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \in [C,D]
              we call
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_! h
              the
              %strong
                left Kan extension of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              along
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %p
              Similarly, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
              has a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %strong right Kan extension
              operation along
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p_* : [C,D] \to [C',D]
            %p or
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ran
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Ran
                      %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ran = Ran_p: [C,D] \to [C',D]
                    \\,.
          %p
            The analogous definition clearly makes sense as stated in other contexts, such as in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C' = *
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the left Kan extension operation forms the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                  of a functor;
              %li
                %p
                  the right Kan extension operation forms the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
                  of a functor.
            %p
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
              in this case sends objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functor"} constant functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_d
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in [C,D]
              any functor,
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi d
                        %mo →
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_d \to F
                  is the same as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
                  over
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to \Delta_d
                  is the same as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
                  under
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %p
              Therefore the natural hom-isomorphisms of the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_! \dashv p^*)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p^* \dashv p_*)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    D(d, p_* F) \simeq Func(\Delta_d, F)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    D(p_! F, d) \simeq Func(F, \Delta_d)
            %p assert that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mo *
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_* F
                  corepresents the
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mo *
                        %mi F
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_* F = \lim_\leftarrow F
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
                  over
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mo !
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_! F
                  represents the
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mo !
                        %mi F
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_! F = \lim_\to F
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %h4#LocalKanExtensions Local Kan extension
          %p
            There is also a
            %em local
            definition of “the Kan extension of a given functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            along
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %em particular
            diagram of shape
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            can have a limit even if not every such diagram does. It is also a special case of the fact discussed at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
            that an adjoint functor can fail to exist completely, but may still be partially defined. If the local Kan extension of every single functor exists for some given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon C\to C'
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p Thus, by the general notion of “partial adjoints”; we say
          #LocalKanExtension.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The local
              %strong left Kan extension
              of a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\in [C,D]
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : C \to C'
              is, if it exists, a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Lan_p\,F : C'\to D
            %p
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi C
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{[C,D]}(F,p^*(-))\cong Hom_{[C',D]}(Lan_p\,F,-)
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} (co)representation
              of the functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi C
                          %mo ,
                          %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{[C,D]}(F,p^*(-))
            %p
              The local definition of right Kan extensions along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is dual.
          %p
            As for adjoints and limits, by the usual logic of representable functors this can equivalently be rephrased in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/adjoint%20functor#UniversalArrows"} universal morphisms
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong
                left Kan extension
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi F
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi Lan
                        %mi p
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan F = Lan_p F
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
                along
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p :C\to C'
                is a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan F : C' \to D
                equipped with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi F
                        %mo :
                        %mi F
                        %mo ⇒
                        %msup
                          %mi p
                          %mo *
                        %mi Lan
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_F : F \Rightarrow p^* Lan F
            %center
              %img{:alt => "", :src => "/nlab/files/kan-0.png"}/
            %p
              with the property that every other natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \Rightarrow p^* G
              factors uniquely through
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_F
              as
            %center
              %img{:alt => "", :src => "/nlab/files/kan-1.png"}/
            %p Similarly for the right Kan extension, with the direction of the natural transformations reversed:
            %center
              %img{:alt => "", :src => "/nlab/files/kan-2.png"}/
          %p
            By the usual reasoning (see e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+Work"} Categories Work
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            then they can be organised into a left (right) adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Lan
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan_p
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ran
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ran_p
            ) to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
          #InHigherCats.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The definition in this form makes sense not just in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              but in every
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:C\to D
              along a 1-cell
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in K(C,C')
              in a 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is a pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi p
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Lan_p F,\alpha)
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi p
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : F\to Lan_p F\circ p
              is a 2-cell which
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflections"} reflects
              the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\in K(C,D)
              along the functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^* = K(p,D):K(C',D)\to K(C,D)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\colon C' \to D
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi p
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi α
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(C',D)(Lan_p F, G) \xrightarrow{- \cdot \alpha} K(C,D)(F, G \circ p)
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            %p
              In this form, the definition generalizes easily to any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} n-category
              for any
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\ge 2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is an
              = succeed "-category," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:C\to D
              along a 1-morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in K(C,C')
              is a pair
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Lan
                        %mi p
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Lan_p F,\alpha)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi p
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan_p F \colon C' \to D
              is a 1-morphism and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi p
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : F\to Lan_p F\circ p
              is a 2-morphism, with the property that for any 1-morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\colon C'\to D
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi p
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi α
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(C',D)(Lan_p F, G) \xrightarrow{- \cdot \alpha} K(C,D)(F, G \circ p)
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
              of
              = succeed "-categories." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-2)
          %h3#Preservation Preservation of Kan extensions
          %p
            We say that a Kan extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Lan
                    %mi p
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan_p F
            is
            %em preserved
            by a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            if the composite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi Lan
                    %mi p
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \circ Lan_p F
            is a Kan extension of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G F
            along
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Lan
                    %mi p
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G F \to G(Lan_p F)p
            is the composite of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with the universal transformation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi p
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\to (Lan_p F)p
          %h3#Pointwise Pointwise Kan extensions
          %p
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            admits certain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} (co)limits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
            out of these: Kan extensions that admit this form are called
            = succeed "." do
              %em pointwise
            = succeed "))." do
              %a{:href => "#Riehl"} Riehl, I 1.3
          %p
            The notion of pointwise Kan extensions deserves to be discussed in the general context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#PointwiseByConicalLimits"} pointwise Kan extensions by conical (co)limits
          %p
            which discusses the situation in ordinary (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"}> Set
            \-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"}> enriched
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            in terms of ordinary limits (“conical” limits, defined in terms of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
            = succeed "s)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %p The general formulation of pointwise Kan extensions in general enriched contexts is
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#PointwiseByWeightedColimits"}> in terms of weighted (co)limits
              \.
          %p
            In the case that the codomain category is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} (co)powered
            these may be expressed equivalently
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#PointwiseByCoEnds"}> in terms of (co)ends
              \.
          %p First, here is a characterization that doesn’t rely on any computational framework:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A Kan extension, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalKanExtension"}
              %strong pointwise
              if and only if it is
              %a{:href => "#Preservation"} preserved
              by all
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
          %p
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+Work"}> Categories Work
            , theorem X.5.3)
          %h4#PointwiseByWeightedColimits In terms of weighted (co)limits
          %p
            Suppose given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : C \to C'
            such that for every
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c' \in C'
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Ran
                    %mi p
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (Ran_p F)(c') \coloneqq lim^{C'(c',p(-))} F
                  \\,.
          %p
            exists. Then these objects fit together into a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ran
                    %mi p
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ran_p F
            which is a right Kan extension of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            along
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted colimit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Lan
                    %mi p
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (Lan_p F)(c') \coloneqq colim^{C'(p(-),c')} F
                  \\,.
          %p
            exists for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c'
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi p
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan_p F
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+equipped+with+proarrows"} 2-category equipped with proarrows
          %p
            In particular, this means that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is
